  "note": "Election of the Newry Urban Council, polled Wednesday 21 May 1958 (Irish News, 23 May 1958, p. 1). The six North Ward seats were filled by six Unionists returned unopposed (Newry Telegraph, 24 May 1958, p. 4). North Ward was uncontested and is not itemised; the new Council was Labour 9, Unionist 6, Irish Citizen Association 3."
